# PowerShell coverage exclusions for the xp-gate pre-commit hook.
#
# One glob per line. Blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored.
# Matched source files are removed from Pester's -CodeCoverage path list.
#
# Current state (2026-10-16, gate-hardening batch 3): this list is EMPTY.
# The root cause of the historical entries — the adapter's coverage
# denominator being a whole-repo `find . -name '*.ps1'` — has been fixed in
# the local adapter (`~/.config/xp-gate/adapters/powershell.sh`): the file
# discovery prune list now covers the xp-gate scaffold dot directories
# (.worktrees/.workbuddy/.sprint-state/.delphi-work/.qoder/.vscode/.idea/
# .xp-gate) plus project-specific entries injected via
# `.xp-gate-powershell-prune-dirs` (this repo: wrc-drill). Measured discovery
# after the fix: 20 test files + 18 product source files (references/scripts
# 17 scripts + setup.ps1) — exactly the baseline, nothing extra, nothing
# excluded. Verified in the batch-3 commit (see docs/audits/2026-10-16
# -gate-status.md, appendix).
#
# Historical entries (removed, with their original rationale kept below for
# the record): wrc-drill/*.ps1, .sprint-state/delphi-run.ps1, .delphi-work/*.
# They were never product code; they are now pruned at discovery time, not
# silently subtracted from the coverage denominator — the denominator stays
# honest (it is the true product file list) instead of being patched per
# artifact.
#
# Do NOT add files here merely because they are hard to test. If a script
# really cannot be instrumented, prove it in the commit message and fix the
# script first (setup.ps1 was exactly that case: a code defect dressed up as
# a structural limit, refactored away in 721cada).
#
# HARD BOUNDARY RULES (do not weaken):
# 1. references/scripts/** and setup.ps1 are PRODUCT CODE and must NEVER be
#    listed here. If they are hard to test, that is a defect to fix, not to
#    exclude.
# 2. Prefer exact file entries over directory globs. A directory-level glob
#    silently exempts anything later dropped into that directory.
# 3. Non-product scratch scripts must NOT be listed here — put the directory
#    into `.xp-gate-powershell-prune-dirs` instead so it leaves discovery,
#    testing, analysis AND the coverage denominator together, in one visible
#    tracked file.
